cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenGEO, cite the repository. Individual rounds carry their own
  dated reports under experiments/results/published/ — cite the round, not
  just the repo, when you are quoting a specific number.
title: "OpenGEO: an open, reproducible, causal benchmark for Generative Engine Optimization"
abstract: >-
  OpenGEO measures whether changing a piece of content changes whether an AI
  answer engine cites it. Documents are supplied to the model in context, so
  retrieval is held constant and the synthesis stage is measured in isolation.
  Every round uses a paired design in which only the document under test differs
  between arms, is pre-registered before collection, and ships its corpus,
  harness and raw model responses so the result can be re-run and checked.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lu
    family-names: Yang
repository-code: "https://github.com/dcefferty/OpenGEO"
url: "https://dcefferty.github.io/OpenGEO/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-04"
keywords:
  - generative engine optimization
  - GEO
  - large language models
  - citation
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - causal inference
